  "description": "A start key typed into USRIDINI: the ELSE at :220-222, which is the only path that anchors the browse on what the operator typed rather than on LOW-VALUES. 'USER0002' is moved into SEC-USR-ID, so the page begins at that key - STARTBR's default positioning is at or after the RIDFLD, and :288 is false for ENTER so the anchor record is kept rather than discarded. Four records remain, so the loop fills rows 1 to 4, the fifth READNEXT reaches the end of the file, and :319-321 counts the short page as page 1. :328 then MOVEs a single SPACE into USRIDINO - padded to eight by the alphanumeric MOVE - so the start-key field is cleared once the page it asked for has been built; :231 covers the same field on the path where :328 was not reached. PROCESS-PAGE-BACKWARD deliberately does not do this, which is why case07's USRIDINO keeps what it was sent.",
